check 1: the battery is good enough
check 2: the image is the declared one and names one root
  the image names its root: system_a
check 3: the stored boot chain is whole and the ssh key is private
step 4: say what to expect
  One command, about 10 minutes: the phone boots our UFS-on image once, from memory; its root is the Alpine system partition of the slot Android is NOT on, mounted READ-ONLY with an overlay in memory. The lab logs in over usb-network by ssh and reads the mounts and the kernel log; NOTHING is written to the card (the partition tables of its 6 disks, the root partition and the boot chain are hashed before and after and must be equal). The glass stays dark. The phone returns to Android by itself; if it is not on Android after 4 minutes, hold the power button about 15 seconds.
step 5: the phone is on Android, adbd as root
check 6: adb reads the slot Android runs from
  adb: slot suffix _b
check 7: the card is read from Android: its partition tables and the root partition
  6 disks and system_a hashed
step 8: take the phone to fastboot
check 9: fastboot agrees on the slot and the image's root is the other one
  the root is system_a; Android runs from slot b
step 10: make this run's image: the declared one with the slot read on its command line
  the run image d594dcbe3efc9c13859bcf3c3c7845967ab95719c79b6cc88fcd75b82e84348f is the declared c3373d7199d26a403a7ac9b10c8c95f4dd17f41d358eb59de095efd6bb6c7ba9 with the slot on its command line (59 bytes differ: the header's command line and, after the content, at most the footer's digest)
check 11: the slots' flags are read
check 12: the author's go is recorded on the item
step 13: boot the UFS-root image from memory, nothing flashed
check 14: USB device 1d6b:0104 is on the bus
step 15: log in over usb-network by ssh and read the phone
check 16: it is root's login on the image, the network and the services are up
  kernel 7.3.0-00013-g3644090c7f6d-dirty
check 17: the init saw the slot adb saw and mounted the named partition
  the init mounted /dev/sda22 (PARTNAME system_a) with slot suffix _b
check 18: the card is mounted read-only under the overlay
  /dev/sda22 is mounted read-only (ro, norecovery, no discard) under the overlay
check 19: the kernel log has no purge, oops or UFS failure
step 20: send the phone back: to its bootloader first, the forced reboot if that is not reached
bootloader reached: fastboot lists the phone, current-slot b equals the slot at the start; fastboot reboot follows
step 21: the phone is on Android (the way back, if it is not)
check 22: the phone is back on Android
rootfs boots on the Pixel 2: stopped at check 22 "the phone is back on Android": not back on Android within 240 s: fail walleye-idle-android host the phone is in fastboot: fastboot reboot, then wait for Android
the run stopped (exit 1)
the phone goes back to Android if it is not there
  6 disks and system_a hashed
measured after the stop: the partition tables and the root partition are as before
measured after the stop: the boot chain are as before
measured after the stop: both slots' flags are as before
